hadiths[8]{hadithnumber,text}:
"16499","Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hisham narrated to us, and Yazid said: Hisham informed us, he said: Yahya narrated to me, from Abu Qilaba, from Thabit ibn al-Dahhak, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Cursing the believer is like killing him. And whoever kills himself with a thing in this world will be punished with it in the Hereafter. And there is no vow upon a Muslim man in what he does not own. And whoever accuses a believer of disbelief, it is like killing him. And whoever swears by a religion other than Islam, lying, it is as he said."
"16500","He said: Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Khalid al-Hadhdha, from Abu Qilaba, from Thabit ibn al-Dahhak al-Ansari, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever swears by a religion other than Islam, lying deliberately, it is as he said. And he said: Whoever kills himself with a thing, Allah will punish him with it in the Fire of Hell."
"16501","He said: Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Harb narrated to us, Yahya narrated to us, he said: Abu Qilabah narrated to me, he said: Thabit ibn al-Dahhak al-Ansari narrated to me, and he was among those who pledged under the tree, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever swears an oath by a religion other than Islam, lying, then he is as he said, and whoever kills himself with something will be punished with it on the Day of Resurrection, and a man has no vow concerning what he does not own."
"16502","He said: Affan narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad narrated to us, Sulayman al-Shaybani narrated to us, Abdullah ibn al-Saib narrated to us, he said: I asked Abdullah ibn Maqil about sharecropping, and he said: Thabit ibn al-Dahhak narrated to us that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade sharecropping."
"16503","He said: Affan narrated to us, he said: Aban narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Abi Kathir narrated to us, from Abu Qilabah, from Thabit ibn al-Dahhak al-Ansari, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever swears by a religion other than Islam, lying, then he is as he said, and a man has no vow concerning what he does not own, and whoever kills himself with something in this world will be punished with it on the Day of Resurrection."
"16504","He said: Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Khalid, from Abu Qilabah, from Thabit ibn al-Dahhak, and he was among the companions of the tree, then he said afterwards, or from a man, from Thabit ibn al-Dahhak, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he said: Whoever swears by a religion other than Islam, lying deliberately, then he is as he said, and whoever kills himself with something, or slaughters himself, Allah will slaughter him with it in the Fire of Hell."
"16505","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Abu Qilabah, from Thabit ibn al-Dahhak, raising the hadith to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: Whoever kills himself with something will be punished with it, and whoever testifies against a Muslim, or he said: a believer, of disbelief, then he is like killing him, and whoever curses him, then it is like killing him, and whoever swears by a religion other than Islam, lying, then he is as he swore."
"16506","Ali ibn Asim narrated to us, from Khalid, from Abu Qilabah, from Thabit ibn al-Dahhak, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever swears by a religion other than Islam, lying deliberately, then he is as he said, and whoever kills himself with something, Allah will punish him with it in the Fire of Hell."
